dio, learning the business is tough. Gina started her venture after losing her job, finding the journey tough but rewarding.\n  - ad campaign: Gina launched an ad campaign for her clothing store to grow the business, which she finds both scary and rewarding.\n  - entrepreneur: Gina and Jon discussed marketing strategies, social media, and influencers. Gina is growing an online store; Jon is promoting his business. They encouraged each other as entrepreneurs.\n  - dance-inspired items: Gina is adding dance-inspired items to her online store to show creativity and share her passion for dance and fashion.\n  - Gina: Gina advises Jon on marketing, is growing her online store, and asked Jon when he is opening his dance studio. She expressed excitement for his studio opening.\n  - Gina: Gina is excited about being noticed by fashion editors. She encourages Jon after he lost his job and is pursuing his business dreams, reminding him of community support.\n  - fashion bloggers: Gina plans to work with fashion bloggers and influencers in the next few months to get more attention for her online store.\n  - relationships: Gina is always working on building relationships and creating a strong brand image for her store.\n  - brand identity: Gina is working on building relationships and creating a strong brand image for her store, acknowledging Jon's advice that these are key.\n  - Gina's customers: Gina's store is designed to be cozy and inviting, featuring trendy pieces to offer customers a special shopping experience. Gina is determined to make it work despite challenges.\n  - wholesalers: Gina emailed wholesalers for her clothing store, and one replied affirmatively, allowing her to expand and get closer to customers.\n  - Gina: Gina is experiencing an exciting but scary time after being noticed by fashion editors. She encourages Jon to keep pursuing his business dreams.\n  - Gina: Gina informed Jon she was accepted for a part-time fashion internship at an international compa