e script submissions.\n  - a hard moment in my life: Joanna wrote an online blog post about 'a hard moment in my life'; someone later wrote her a letter saying the story brought them comfort.\n  - seeing all of the characters and dialogue I wrote being acted out: Joanna experienced seeing all of the characters and dialogue she wrote being acted out, which was rewarding and the third time this has happened to her.\n  - picture: Nate complimented Joanna's drawings, asking what inspired them. Joanna previously mentioned seeing her writing acted out and Nate complimented a hiking picture.\n  - Jo: Joanna (Jo) asked Nate if he celebrated good feedback people are connecting with his writing. Previously, she asked about a couple he met while walking Max.\n  - script: Joanna is filming a movie from her road-trip script. An actor praised the script, making Joanna excited and giving her chills.\n  - letter: Joanna received a letter last week from someone who read her online blog post about a hard moment; the writer felt comfort from her story. Nate commented that the letter is really awesome.\n  - old notebooks: Joanna found old notebooks containing her early writings last week, showing her progress. Nate asked Joanna what she was working on in that notebook.\n  - screenplay: Joanna wrote parts of a screenplay that appeared on the big screen yesterday and submitted a recent screenplay to a film contest.\n  - movies: Joanna highly rates movies (9-10/10) for emotional impact. Nate suggested watching one of Joanna's movies together.\n  - audition: Joanna had an audition for a writing gig yesterday; she feels mixed emotions but is excited, and Nate wished her luck.\n  - movie: Joanna is filming her movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and enjoys showing her vision, with Nate asking about the coolest moment.\n  - this: Nate won a large video game tournament last week, earning a lot of money from it. Joanna congratulated him.\n  - drama: Joanna fe