-06T15:56:00Z)\n  - Solar is an example of renewable energy that Jolene is focusing on for a project. (event_time: 2023-08-26T17:33:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - electrical engineering project: Jolene finished an electrical engineering project last week after a lot of work.\n  - it: Jolene finished a tough engineering project last month and is proud of sticking it out despite problems, considering it a big milestone.\n  - milestone: Jolene finished a tough engineering project last month, calling it a big milestone she is proud of, having stuck it out despite problems. Deborah congratulated her.\n  - big project: Jolene has been working on a big project that is tough but cool to watch take shape, and she anticipates the final result.\n  - engineer: Jolene, an engineer, is coping with an emotional rollercoaster but achieved a major milestone last week, causing relief and pride. She later asked Deborah for an explanation.\n  - robotics project: Jolene's engineering professor assigned a huge robotics project. Jolene finds it tough but fun, enjoying the problem-solving and seeing the robot assemble.\n  - engineering skills: Jolene's engineering skills led to a major milestone accomplishment last week, making a positive difference for people in a rural area.\n  - Battlefield 1: Jolene received the new console game Battlefield 1 last week and mentioned it to Deborah.\n  - setback with Jolene's project: Jolene experienced a huge setback with her project last week, causing her to lose all her work, which was frustrating and depressing. Deborah offered support.\n  - Detroit: Jolene and her partner played the game \"Detroit\" on the console last week and are both crazy about gaming.\n  - projects: Jolene is interested in projects that make a real difference, specifically sustainable initiatives and innovative environmental solutions, integrating values from loved ones.\n  - career aspirations: Deborah a