e game. James asked John about new game designs.\n  - John: John plays drums, recently chatted with James about a new RPG with a cool story and tough gameplay, which sometimes causes lag and errors.\n  - John: John is loving sharing his coding journey and tracking everything. He also bought many new books, almost completely filling his bookcase.\n  - game: Three days ago, James lost power during a game (Mario). John collaborated with a developer on an online board game and was asked if it has been released.\n  - John: John started a startup making portable smokers, welding one prototype. He is launching a 2D adventure game soon and recently held a Fortnite gaming tourney to raise funds for a children's hospital.\n  - John: John started playing the board game \"Dungeons of the Dragon\". Previously, John volunteered programming skills for a charitable foundation and got his dream job.\n  - John: John volunteered for a charitable foundation creating software. He recently placed second in a local tournament last Friday, noting the competitive energy was insane.\n  - John: John collaborated with a game developer to create a unique online board game and ended a conversation with James about it. Previously, he won a chess tournament and organized charity gaming tournaments.\n  - John: John plays drums, won a game, and attended a gaming convention. He congratulated James on winning an online gaming tournament.\n  - John: John commiserated with James about losing power during a game and offered to send him resources and tutorials on new programming approaches.\n  - notes: James writes down what he needs to do in a notebook to help him remember things. John expressed interest in seeing sketches or notes from exploring a castle.\n  - John: John is working on a cool coding project with his siblings, which is a game to help them learn. He is also working on his first professional website for a small business.\n  - John: John organized an online programming competition and expressed gratitude for James' support. He was told about James losing power during a game and asked about a seminar he attended.\n  - John: John started playing board games, trying \"Dungeons of the Dragon.\" He enjoys electronic and rock music and used to play drums. He left his 3-year IT job for a new one aligned with his values.\n  - game developers: John recently collaborated with a game developer to create an online board game, bringing his ideas to life. Previously, John mentored game developers in coding.\n  - John: John organized a CS:GO tournament that raised money for charity. He also volunteered programming skills to create a software tool for a charitable foundation to streamline operations.\n  - John: John is excited to start volunteering as a programming mentor for a game dev non-profit, teaching coding and assisting with projects. He is meeting with James.\n  - game world: James created a game and released it. He felt fulfillment seeing players engage with the game world he created, which inspired John to ask about its creation.\n  - programming projects: John asked James about what motivates him for programming projects; James later worked on a virtual world inspired by Witcher 3 with a gaming pal.\n  - mobile game: John achieved a major career milestone by creating a mobile game, which James learned about after congratulating him.\n  - game development: John congratulated James on releasing his game and praised his determination and love for game development, anticipating future creations.\n  - John: John collaborated with a game developer on an online board game and appreciates dogs for the joy and positivity they bring.\n  - John: John is working on his first professional website project for a local small business and is currently playing AC Valhalla.\n  - James: James chatted with John about work and asked what games John was playing.\n  - blog about coding: John started a blog about coding last week, finding it awesome and challenging. He enjoys shar