ewarding. Nate inquired about the character on the left in a shared photo.\n  - Jo: Joanna (Jo) asked Nate if he celebrated good feedback people are connecting with his writing. Previously, she asked about a couple he met while walking Max.\n  - literature: Joanna advises reading lots, trying different genres, and writing/sharing literature to build understanding and improve through practice and feedback.\n  - the town: Joanna visited the town of Woodhaven, a small town in the Midwest known for lovely scenery and historic buildings. She found a cool old book from the 1900s in the library there.\n  - writers group: Joanna shared her book with her writers group last week and received great feedback. She recently finished a cute little bookmark for one of the ladies at her writing club.\n  - movie script: Joanna is filming a movie based on her road-trip script. She previously hoped for big-screen distribution, and Nate asked about future script submissions.\n  - old notebooks: Joanna found old notebooks containing her early writings last week, showing her progress. Nate asked Joanna what she was working on in that notebook.\n  - bookmark: Joanna finished a cute little bookmark for a lady at her writing club. Nate commented that the bookmark is great and she will love it.\n  - \"The Lord of the Rings\" Trilogy: Joanna watched \"The Lord of the Rings\" Trilogy after Nate's recommendation and found it awesome. Nate considered it the greatest trilogy of all time.\n  - keepsakes: Joanna shared a picture of her cork board, which contains quotes, photos, and little keepsakes.\n  - insects: Insects are part of a varied diet eaten by something, which also includes vegetables and fruits, according to Joanna.\n  - living room: Nate asked Joanna for pointers on what to get for his living room to make it comfy. Joanna responded positively, and Nate plans to try out her suggestions.\n  - things: Nate asked Joanna what other things she is making when she is in a certain mood.\n  - pi