d about Calvin's Frank Ocean tour experience and managing fame. Dave also discussed having a helpful conversation with neighbors about current events and politics.\n  - Dave: Dave previously enjoyed a card night and is restoring a car for his auto engineering goal. He chatted with Calvin about Calvin's amazing performance on a big stage.\n  - House of Blues: Dave told Calvin that House of Blues is a cool music spot in Boston that Calvin should check out when he visits.\n  - Dave: Dave congratulated Calvin on his album release and expressed enthusiasm for live music. Dave invited Calvin to see his cool cars in his garage.\n  - Dave: Dave greeted Calvin, mentioned taking up photography (scenery pics), complimented Calvin's gala appearance, and noted his camera captures moments clearly.\n  - flight ticket: Calvin booked a flight ticket to Boston last week and is excited about the upcoming trip.\n  - Dave: Dave asked Calvin about his car post-crash, mentioned arranging regular walks with friends in parks, and commented on a mansion's stunning view in Japan.\n  - team: Calvin mentioned his team is part of his strong support system that helps him manage his overwhelming job demands. He was also with his crew at a fancy gala in Boston.\n  - Dave: Dave inquired about Calvin's tour with Frank Ocean, the impact of fame on relationships, and how Calvin manages his job and personal life.\n  - ramen: Dave mentioned that the food in Tokyo is great and that he will have fun exploring different places, asking if Calvin has tried ramen yet. Dave also shared a photo of ramen he tried in Boston.\n  - Dave: Dave congratulated Calvin on his new album party, asked about the cheering, and commented that music can affect mood and help stay on track.\n  - Dave: Dave, who is restoring a vintage Mustang engine, has taken up photography, focusing on local scenery. He discussed his photography and the car project with Calvin.\n  - collaborations: Calvin started touring with Frank Ocean after th